### 1. List Customers (Paginated, Searchable, Filterable)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/v1/customers?page=1&limit=10&status=LEAD&sortBy=createdAt&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>

### 2. Search Customers by Keyword (matches name, mobile, businessName, email)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/v1/customers?q=Apex
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>

### 3. Create New Customer
POST http://localhost:5000/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Zenith Enterprises",
  "mobile": "+919988776655",
  "email": "contact@zenith.com",
  "businessName": "Zenith Corp Pvt Ltd",
  "gstNumber": "27ZZZZZ9999Z9Z9",
  "customerType": "DISTRIBUTOR",
  "address": "404 Tech Park, Pune, MH",
  "status": "LEAD"
}

### 4. Get Customer Detail
GET http://localhost:5000/api/v1/customers/<CUSTOMER_ID>
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>

### 5. Update Customer (PATCH)
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/v1/customers/<CUSTOMER_ID>
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "email": "updated@zenith.com"
}

### 6. Add Follow-Up Note to Customer
POST http://localhost:5000/api/v1/customers/<CUSTOMER_ID>/notes
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Discussed bulk ordering discounts over phone call. Customer agreed to place trial order next week."
}

### 7. Get All Notes for Customer
GET http://localhost:5000/api/v1/customers/<CUSTOMER_ID>/notes
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>
